[b]Change the gear of your own troops.[/b]

Open any troop in the [b]Encyclopedia[/b] - say the Battanian Volunteer - press [b]Edit gear[/b] and swap his weapons, armour or horse slot by slot. Only troops of [b]your[/b] parties wear your version: your party, your clan's parties and your garrisons. Everyone else in Calradia keeps the vanilla gear.

[size=5][b]What it does[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]A troop has several vanilla gear sets. Edit each set on its own, or press [b]All sets[/b] on a slot to put that item on every set.
[*][b]Reset[/b] one slot, [b]Reset this set[/b], or [b]Reset whole unit to vanilla[/b].
[*]The item picker shows each item's tier and price, and filters by tier, culture and type, or by name.
[*]On the Encyclopedia page of an edited troop, switch between [b]Vanilla[/b] and [b]My version[/b].
[*]The party screen shows your troops in their new gear.
[*]Edits are free and instant, anywhere on the map. Sets you leave alone keep the game's random variety.
[*]Works with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3674824323]Troop Equipment Upgrade[/url]: it still sees the vanilla troop and prices upgrades as before.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/2006]Harmony[/url] (required)
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/2102]UIExtenderEx[/url] (required)
[/list]

[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Vortex:[/b] click Mod Manager Download and enable it.
[*][b]Manual:[/b] extract the zip into [i]Mount & Blade II Bannerlord\Modules\[/i], so you get [i]Modules\MyTroopsGear\SubModule.xml[/i]. Enable it in the launcher, below Harmony and UIExtenderEx.
[/list]

[size=5][b]Good to know[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Game v1.4.8, singleplayer. Works with or without War Sails.
[*]Safe to add or remove mid-campaign.
[*]Not for troops that another mod rewrites ([url=https://www.nexusmods.com/mountandblade2bannerlord/mods/3164]My Little Warband[/url] and the like): both would change the same soldier.
[*]Gear counts in battles you fight (field, siege, hideout, at sea). Auto-resolve does not look at gear.
[*]Formations stay as they are: a spearman you give a bow or a horse still lines up as infantry.
[*]Heroes, prisoners, tournaments and the arena stay vanilla.
[*]Also on [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/my-troops-gear/releases/latest]GitHub Releases[/url]. Same files.
[/list]

The idea of an in-game gear editor comes from My Little Warband. This mod is written from scratch and uses none of its code or files.

Bugs or a mod it fights with: tell me in the comments or on [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/my-troops-gear/issues]GitHub[/url]. How it works in detail: [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/my-troops-gear/blob/main/docs/TECHNICAL.md]docs/TECHNICAL.md[/url].

Made by two of us: the code and all technical work by Claude (Opus 5.5), an AI; the idea, feedback and playtesting by [url=https://github.com/TraxData313]Trax[/url], Bible believer and engineer in AI/ML/Python/Applied Maths.

Free and open — public domain (The Unlicense). Source: [url=https://github.com/TraxData313/my-troops-gear]github.com/TraxData313/my-troops-gear[/url]
To thank me, open [url=https://github.com/TraxData313]my GitHub profile[/url] and read my top pinned.
